---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import LimitChecker from '../../components/LimitChecker.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Character & Word Limit Checker"
  description="Check your text against common character limits — tweets, SMS, meta descriptions, title tags, and more — all at once."
>
  <LimitChecker client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why check against multiple limits at once</h2>
  <p>
    Content often gets reused across platforms — a product description
    might become a tweet, a meta description, and an SMS notification. This
    tool checks your text against several common limits simultaneously, so
    you know at a glance where it fits and where it needs trimming.
  </p>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Why does SMS count differently?</strong> Standard SMS messages
    are limited to 160 characters per segment; longer messages get split
    into multiple segments (and billed accordingly) by carriers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Are these limits always accurate?</strong> Platform limits
    change over time — these reflect commonly cited values as of this
    writing. Always verify against the platform's current official limit
    for anything critical.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
